# A pull from stdin in a token action. Backing up gives the text back to
# stdin, which the program can read from between sends.
lex
	token id /[a-z]+/
	literal `;
	ignore /[ \n]+/

	token at /'@'/
	{
		input->pull( 1 )
		input->push( stdin->pull( 1 ) )
	}
end

def start
	[id* `;]

P: parser<start> = new parser<start>()
send P "a @ ;" eos
##### COMP_ERR #####
11:16: cannot change stdin, a global, in an action of a restartable parser: keep the data in a context
